{
 "id": "2021-zhang-community",
 "name": "Community Park Elements: View and Rank Preference",
 "description": "Faithful replication with the paper's own stimuli: participants watch 35 photographs of landscape elements in Shanghai community parks (10 s each, 5 s black screen between), then rank the photos within each of nine element groups (amount of greenery, plant colour, waterscapes, fitness facilities, fitness trails, activity spaces, seats, pavilions and corridors, green corridors) from most to least liked. Answers are keyed by scene id, so mean ranks per scene can be compared with the paper's preference scores (Tables 8–16 of Zhang, Liu & Liu 2021, IJERPH 18(15): 7888; photos CC BY 4.0). Differences from the original study: (1) online instead of a quiet lab, with no heart-rate or skin-conductance recording and no 3-minute rest; (2) photos are the small versions printed in the paper's tables; (3) viewing order and group order are random per participant; (4) the paper only says participants \"prioritized the landscape scenes\", so ranking within each group by tapping is our implementation; (5) the separate park-user questionnaire (440 users) is not included; age and gender questions are added.",
